  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle. Cut potato into bite-sized chunks.\n• Half-fill a medium saucepan with the boiled water. Add chicken-style stock powder and heat over medium-high heat.\n• Cook potato in the boiling water until easily pierced with a fork, 12-15 minutes.\n• Drain potato, then return to pan. Add the butter and dill & parsley mayonnaise. Crumble in fetta cubes. Toss to combine and season to taste. Cover to keep warm.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/633663d69f16fd2cb704c55e/step-a6be3ac1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• SPICY! The spice blend is mild, but use less if you're sensitive to heat. While the potato is cooking, cut haloumi into 1cm-thick slices.\n• Combine All-American spice blend, a pinch of salt and pepper and a drizzle of olive oil in a medium bowl. Add haloumi, tossing to coat.\n• In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. Cook haloumi until golden brown, 1-2 minutes each side. TIP: The spice blend will char slightly in the pan, this adds to the flavour!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/633663d69f16fd2cb704c55e/step-11e1e281.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• While the haloumi is cooking, thinly slice apple into wedges. Roughly chop baby spinach leaves.\n• In a second medium bowl, combine a drizzle of white wine vinegar and olive oil. Season, then add slaw mix, apple and spinach. Toss to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/633663d69f16fd2cb704c55e/step-39b8685f.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide American-spiced haloumi and warm potato-fetta salad between plates.\n• Serve with apple slaw. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/633663d69f16fd2cb704c55e/step-1ce2b274.jpg"
    }
  ]
